From 5c2cb84c81bb2a5a99c4c8973244597dce374daf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: greyoak111 <151205158+greyoak111@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 23:55:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/43] Pick the RTMP endpoint deterministically when going
 live

startLive can list several protocols. The endpoint parser inherited from
v0.1.2 took whichever nested dictionary value it met first; Swift
dictionary order is random per run, so when that was the SRT entry the
room opened but going live failed with a generic server error. Prefer
data.rtmp and protocols[rtmp], then collect candidates in sorted key order
and take the first rtmp/rtmps one. If the room opened without a usable
endpoint, fall back to GetUpStreamRtmp. Server-kind errors now show their
technical reason in the dock.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
